        "category": "correctness",
        "consequence": "Any code that reads `queued` sees the process start time instead of the real queue time. The value gets staler the longer a worker runs. It is also serialized into the task kwargs via `to_dict`.",
        "evidence_refs": [
          "source:new:src/sentry/integrations/services/assignment_source.py@sha256:885ab5f3b8ef5398cf84e90112d9352978908c663d9034ef89e7ed4eccfdfa0e",
          "target:target:sym:e2667472e8f5513cf4f56a3f"
        ],
        "explanation": "The field `queued: datetime = timezone.now()` calls `timezone.now()` once, when the class body runs at module import. Every `AssignmentSource` built without an explicit `queued`, including all those from `from_integration`, gets that same import-time timestamp. The timestamp does not show when the assignment was queued. A `default_factory` is needed so each instance gets its own time.",
        "lines": {
